@startuml
title Jenkins + Docker + Flutter CI Architecture

start

' ============================================================
' HOST PREPARATION (WSL2)
' ============================================================

note
Run once on WSL2 host:

    sudo ./jenkins_setup_host_dirs.sh

Or manually:
end note

note
Prepare persistent host directories:

cd ~
sudo rm -rf /home/mirko/jenkins_host_*

sudo mkdir -p /home/mirko/jenkins_host_workspace
sudo mkdir -p /home/mirko/jenkins_host_workspace/artifacts

sudo chown -R 2000:2000 /home/mirko/jenkins_host_workspace
sudo chmod -R 770 /home/mirko/jenkins_host_workspace


sudo mkdir -p /home/mirko/jenkins_host_cache/gradle
sudo mkdir -p /home/mirko/jenkins_host_cache/pub
sudo mkdir -p /home/mirko/jenkins_host_cache/cargo

sudo chown -R 2000:2000 /home/mirko/jenkins_host_cache
sudo chmod -R 770 /home/mirko/jenkins_host_cache
end note

note
Restart infrastructure:

docker compose down
docker compose up -d --build
end note


' ============================================================
' FLUTTER ANDROID BUILD STACK
' ============================================================

note
Flutter Android build flow:

• Flutter → compiles Dart
• Gradle → builds Android APK/AAB
• Kotlin → native Android layer
• Maven → dependency resolution
end note


' ============================================================
' DOCKER CLEANUP REFERENCE
' ============================================================

note
------------------------------------------------------------
DOCKER CLEANUP REFERENCE
------------------------------------------------------------
end note


note
docker builder prune

Removes:
• BuildKit layer cache
• Intermediate build layers

Keeps:
• Images
• Containers
• Volumes
• Networks
end note


note
docker builder prune --all -f

Removes:
• ALL build cache (all builders)

Keeps:
• Images
• Containers
• Volumes
• Networks
end note


note
docker image prune -f

Removes:
• Dangling (untagged) images

Keeps:
• Tagged images
• Containers
• Volumes
end note


note
docker image prune -a -f

Removes:
• ALL unused images

Keeps:
• Images used by containers
• Volumes
end note


note
docker system prune -f

Removes:
• Stopped containers
• Unused networks
• Dangling images
• Build cache

Keeps:
• Named volumes
• Images used by containers
end note


note
docker system prune -a -f

Removes:
• Stopped containers
• ALL unused images
• Unused networks
• Build cache

Keeps:
• Named volumes
end note


note
docker system prune -a --volumes -f

⚠ DANGEROUS

Removes:
• Stopped containers
• ALL unused images
• Unused networks
• ALL unused volumes
• Build cache

WARNING:
Deletes persisted data in volumes
end note


note
docker buildx prune --all --force

Removes:
• All buildx cache storage
• Multi-platform builder cache

Keeps:
• Images
• Containers
• Volumes
end note


note
FULL FACTORY RESET

docker system prune -af --volumes

Removes:
• ALL stopped containers
• ALL unused images
• ALL unused networks
• ALL unused volumes
• ALL build cache

Keeps:
• Running containers only
end note


stop
@enduml
